HEADLINE: SCRAMBLER ALLOWS FBI WIRETAPS

BYLINE: From THE PHOENIX GAZETTE news services.

DATELINE: WASHINGTON

BODY:

The White House is touting a new telephone scrambling device, more
sophisticated than anything now on the market, which will provide
state-of-the-art protection against eavesdropping.

The " Clipper Chip" unveiled Friday, is being released by the
government for private use. But unlike other encryptors, this one was
built to enable wiretaps if necessary.

The White House said the device developed by the National Institute of
Standards and Technology would provide new protection against
eavesdropping on corporate secrets. But it also would provide for FBI
access if criminal activity were suspected.

AT&T, which makes security devices, said it would immediately start
putting the new technology in its products.

